-- name    : InertialAVD.Algo.eq_69
-- status  : Open
-- author  : @mikedeng1
-- created : 2026-10-07T21:08:32.480977+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/2facfdf8-2427-42b2-90a2-b4552e1f39c7
-- title:
--   (69) — perturbed descent $\Theta(x_{k+1})+\frac{1}{2s}\|x_{k+1}-x_k\|^2\le\Theta(x_k)+\frac{(k-1)^2}{2s(k+\alpha-1)^2}\|x_k-x_{k-1}\|^2+\langle g_k,x_{k+1}-x_k\rangle$
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal H$ be a real Hilbert space, let $\Phi:\mathcal H\to\mathbb R\cup\{+\infty\}$ be proper, lower semicontinuous and convex, and let $\Psi:\mathcal H\to\mathbb R$ be convex and continuously differentiable with $L$-Lipschitz continuous gradient; write $\Theta=\Phi+\Psi$. Let $s>0$ with $sL<1$, let $(g_k)_{k\ge 0}$ be a sequence of perturbations in $\mathcal H$, and let $(x_k)_{k\ge0},(y_k)_{k\ge0}$ be generated by the perturbed inertial forward-backward algorithm (55):
--
--   $$y_k = x_k + \frac{k-1}{k+\alpha-1}(x_k-x_{k-1})\ (k\ge 1),\qquad x_{k+1}=\operatorname{prox}_{s\Phi}\big(y_k-s(\nabla\Psi(y_k)-g_k)\big)\ (k\ge 0),$$
--
--   with $y_0\in\mathcal H$ arbitrary.
--
--   Assume $\alpha\ge3$. Then for every $k\ge1$,
--
--   $$\Theta(x_{k+1})+\frac{1}{2s}\|x_{k+1}-x_k\|^2\le\Theta(x_k)+\frac{1}{2s}\,\frac{(k-1)^2}{(k+\alpha-1)^2}\,\|x_k-x_{k-1}\|^2+\langle g_k,\,x_{k+1}-x_k\rangle .$$
--
--   This descent inequality controls the velocities $x_{k+1}-x_k$; summed with weights $(k+\alpha-1)^2$ it leads to (70)–(72) and to item ii) of Theorem 5.3.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** $\Phi$ is `EReal`-valued with `IsProperClosedConvex`; $\operatorname{prox}_{s\Phi}$ is a map $P$ with `IsProx s Φ P`; $\Theta$ is the published `NesterovFB.Rates.theta Φ Ψ` (whose argument names are swapped relative to this paper: its first argument is the nonsmooth part). $L$ is a nonnegative real and "$0<s<1/L$" is written $0<s$, $sL<1$, so $L=0$ is allowed. The run is `IsPerturbedRun`. The page derives (69) inside the proof of Theorem 5.3 ($\alpha>3$); the statement assumes only $\alpha\ge3$, which the derivation needs. It holds for $k\ge1$, where $x_{k-1}$ is defined. Both sides are extended reals.
-- source:
--   Attouch, Chbani, Peypouquet, Redont, Fast convergence of inertial dynamics and algorithms with asymptotic vanishing damping, Optimization Online preprint 5179 (Oct. 2015), p. 21, (69)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ThreeOpSplitting_ConvexRates_Problem
import Definitions.Def_NesterovFB_Rates_Algorithm
import Definitions.Def_InertialAVD_Algo_PerturbedRun

open Filter Topology NesterovFB.Rates

namespace InertialAVD.Algo

/-- (69), p. 21: the perturbed descent inequality. For every `k ≥ 1`,
`Θ(x_{k+1}) + ‖x_{k+1} − x_k‖²/(2s) ≤ Θ(x_k) + (k−1)²/(k+α−1)² · ‖x_k − x_{k−1}‖²/(2s)
  + ⟨g_k, x_{k+1} − x_k⟩`. -/
theorem eq_69 {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H] [CompleteSpace H]
    (Φ : H → EReal) (Ψ : H → ℝ) (L : NNReal) (s α : ℝ) (P : H → H) (g : ℕ → H) (x y : ℕ → H)
    (hΦ : ThreeOpSplitting.ConvexRates.IsProperClosedConvex Φ)
    (hΨc : ConvexOn ℝ Set.univ Ψ) (hΨd : ContDiff ℝ 1 Ψ)
    (hL : LipschitzWith L (gradient Ψ))
    (hs : 0 < s) (hsL : s * (L : ℝ) < 1)
    (hP : ThreeOpSplitting.ConvexRates.IsProx s Φ P)
    (hrun : IsPerturbedRun Ψ P α s g x y)
    (hα : 3 ≤ α) :
    ∀ k : ℕ, 1 ≤ k →
      theta Φ Ψ (x (k + 1)) + ((‖x (k + 1) - x k‖ ^ 2 / (2 * s) : ℝ) : EReal)
        ≤ theta Φ Ψ (x k)
          + ((((k : ℝ) - 1) ^ 2 / ((k : ℝ) + α - 1) ^ 2 * ‖x k - x (k - 1)‖ ^ 2 / (2 * s)
              + inner ℝ (g k) (x (k + 1) - x k) : ℝ) : EReal) := by sorry

end InertialAVD.Algo
